{# The page answering every request until the first service is configured. #}
{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block content %}
<header>
<img alt="EasyHAProxy" src="data:image/png;base64,{{ logo }}">
<div>
<h1>EasyHAProxy is running</h1>
<p class="lead">No service is configured yet. This page goes away as soon as the first one is.</p>
</div>
</header>
<section>
<h2>Kubernetes</h2>
Create an Ingress with <code>ingressClassName: easyhaproxy</code>.
<a href="https://opensource.byjg.com/docs/devops/docker-easy-haproxy/getting-started/kubernetes">Kubernetes guide</a>
</section>
<section>
<h2>Docker and Docker Swarm</h2>
Add <code>easyhaproxy.*</code> labels to a container or service.
<a href="https://opensource.byjg.com/docs/devops/docker-easy-haproxy/getting-started/docker">Docker guide</a> &middot;
<a href="https://opensource.byjg.com/docs/devops/docker-easy-haproxy/getting-started/swarm">Swarm guide</a>
</section>
<section>
<h2>Static</h2>
Describe the services in a YAML file.
<a href="https://opensource.byjg.com/docs/devops/docker-easy-haproxy/getting-started/static">Static guide</a>
</section>
<section>
<h2>HTTPS</h2>
Use your own certificates or get them from Let's Encrypt.
<a href="https://opensource.byjg.com/docs/devops/docker-easy-haproxy/guides/ssl">SSL guide</a> &middot;
<a href="https://opensource.byjg.com/docs/devops/docker-easy-haproxy/guides/acme">ACME guide</a>
</section>
<footer>
All labels and annotations: <a href="https://opensource.byjg.com/docs/devops/docker-easy-haproxy/reference/container-labels">reference</a>.
Full documentation: <a href="https://opensource.byjg.com/docs/devops/docker-easy-haproxy/">opensource.byjg.com</a>.
</footer>
{% endblock %}
